{% comment %}
  Renders a swatch component.
  Accepts:
  - swatch: {Object} a swatch object
  - shape: {String} swatch shape. Accepts 'square', defaults to circle.
  - metal: {String} Cullinan: a material value's name, drawn as its metal when the swatch is empty (optional)

  Usage:
  {% render 'swatch',
    swatch: value.swatch
    shape: 'square'
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign swatch_value = null
  if swatch.image
    comment
      Cullinan (2026-10-22, owner: „the quality of the color circles is bad“): Dawn asked for a 50px-wide file, which a
      wide picture makes even shorter, so a 20px circle on a 2-3x phone screen was enlarged and blurred. Now a 160px
      square, cut around the picture's focal point: sharp up to a 53px circle on a 3x screen.
    endcomment
    assign image_url = swatch.image | image_url: width: 160, height: 160, crop: 'center'
    assign swatch_value = 'url(' | append: image_url | append: ')'
    assign swatch_focal_point = swatch.image.presentation.focal_point
  elsif swatch.color
    assign swatch_value = 'rgb(' | append: swatch.color.rgb | append: ')'
  elsif metal != blank
    comment
      Cullinan (2026-10-28): a material value with no swatch of its own draws its metal's circle (cj-metal-swatch).
    endcomment
    capture swatch_value
      render 'cj-metal-swatch', name: metal
    endcapture
    assign swatch_value = swatch_value | strip
    if swatch_value == ''
      assign swatch_value = null
    endif
  endif
-%}

<span
  {% if swatch_value %}
    class="swatch{% if shape == 'square' %} swatch--square{% endif %}"
    style="--swatch--background: {{ swatch_value }};{% if swatch_focal_point %} --swatch-focal-point: {{ swatch_focal_point }};{% endif %}"
  {% else %}
    class="swatch swatch--unavailable{% if shape == 'square' %} swatch--square{% endif %}"
  {% endif %}
></span>
